/-!
# Hyperbolic Arakelov Theory of `Spec ℤ`

Umbrella for the Arakelov geometry of the surface of `Spec ℤ` whose archimedean fibre is `ℍ³` with
the degree geodesic: image distances in Arakelov coordinates; the carriers of B118′ — dilation limits
of twisted carriers, carriers of bounded geometry, along a loxodromic axis and along an end of bounded
self-energy (conical ends included), the boundary of a group convergent at `½` (no parabolic elements,
points of discontinuity), and embeddings into compact and finite-volume quotients; the spherical
structure of the archimedean compensation and the plastic crossing; the discriminant diagonal of
locked dampings; the mass obstruction to scalar locking and ordered Gram coupling on smooth packets;
the finite places as Bruhat–Tits trees with the adelic Green formula; the arithmetic-unit obstruction
to descending a degree ladder and its reconstruction from positive twisted tree fibres; a discrete
adelic arithmetic group whose finite Weyl conjugate retains the original square degrees; and the
weight of the orientation cover over ℤ. See `HyperbolicArakelovTheory/README.md`.
-/
